== perimeter (k=0): P = pi a_0 ; compare tau-series with D11's exact f_n ==
tau-coefficient of P/(4 sqrt2) is e_n = (-1)^n (f_n + f_{n-1}); its set of weights, and pi*c_n(0) - 4sqrt2 e_n:
n= 1: weights [0]  e_n = 0
n= 2: weights [2]  e_n = Z2/4   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 0.0
n= 3: weights [3]  e_n = Z3/4   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 3.11e-61
n= 4: weights [4]  e_n = -7*Z2**2/32 + Z4/32   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 3.11e-61
n= 5: weights [5]  e_n = -7*Z2*Z3/16 - 3*Z5/16   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 6.22e-61
n= 6: weights [6]  e_n = ...   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 0.0
n= 7: weights [7]  e_n = ...   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 4.98e-60
n= 8: weights [8]  e_n = ...   |pi c_n(0) - 4 sqrt2 e_n| = 3.98e-59
n= 9: weights [9]  e_n = ...
n=10: weights [10]  e_n = ...
for contrast, D11's f_n themselves have weights: {2: [0, 2], 3: [0, 2, 3], 4: [0, 2, 3, 4], 5: [0, 2, 3, 4, 5]}

== uniform (boundary-layer) form: a_k ~ A_k + (-1)^k (sqrt2/pi)[1/(4k^2) - pi tau/(2k sinh(2 pi k tau))] ==
